# What a generated project runs on macOS and Linux, as SHA-256 over each file's bytes, written by
# scripts/fence.py. A line changes only with a reason appended below it, saying why what the file does on
# macOS and Linux is unchanged (docs/windows-plan.md, D2). Each reason carries the digest of the record it
# vouches for; editing a line by hand breaks that.
#
# why: 2026-11-09 7406116f1e78db81 The fence is put up over today's tree, before any change for Windows.
# why: 2026-11-09 001fff112e2f6aa5 24.4: models.py and benchmark.py start their sibling scripts with PYTHON, which is "python3" wherever sys.platform is not win32 — the argv macOS and Linux ran before.
# why: 2026-11-09 a89a3c4b51ee4793 24.5: init passes --script sh to Spec Kit only where uname -s says MINGW, MSYS or CYGWIN; on Darwin and Linux the case matches nothing and specify gets the arguments it had.
# why: 2026-11-09 628ad48c4fc19d99 24.8: try_it ends an app's group through end_tree, os.killpg with the same signals off Windows; moorings links through link_folder and is_link, os.symlink and is_symlink off Windows (isjunction is False there); the harbourmaster's symlink_to line is unchanged off Windows.
# why: 2026-11-09 16780b2335a643ce 24.11: the event model's npm install runs as 'cd scripts/event-model && npm install' instead of 'npm --prefix scripts/event-model install', which npm on Windows ignores; each recipe line is its own shell, so the same tree is installed in the same place on macOS and Linux.
# why: 2026-11-09 d2a8de915041746c 24.3: the root Makefile sets .SHELLFLAGS := -hc inside ifeq ($(OS),Windows_NT); OS is unset on macOS and Linux, so the block is skipped and SHELL := /bin/bash runs every line as before.
# why: 2026-11-09 5b5c6f2aa0d51bd8 Off Windows: moorings.leave removes a junction only on os.name nt, and the harbourmaster's refused-rebase message adds git's own last line where it named no file; neither changes what runs on macOS or Linux.
# why: 2026-11-10 7d4301fb5aae4164 Not Windows work, and deliberately a change on every platform: check-slice-scope lets a slice write specs/<feature>/people/ (sail.md rung 12 already told it to) and, on the event profile, the chart check-chart holds to the model, as it lets model.drawio through; logs.py refuses a fleet-ticked need with no check on write and reads one already written as a person's, as fleet.py tell already refused it.
# why: 2026-11-10 f81a3ff6cd1ddce5 Not Windows work, and deliberately a change on every platform: under /cruise the captain resumes a parked slice as answered by decisions only when its newest park was waiting on questions undecided when it was written, the rule the harbourmaster already clears by; a park written after the decisions no longer re-dispatches the slice every turn.
# why: 2026-11-10 3136b0a202ff0d6f harbourmaster: a remote with no trunk yet is given trunk by the first merge, instead of every merge staying local; a remote that has trunk, and a harbour with none, are unchanged
# why: 2026-11-10 d1f1f2c4da4a92cc moorings.berth tries git worktree add again only when git refused over a sibling's half-made .git/worktrees entry; a successful add, and every other refusal, does exactly what it did
# why: 2026-11-10 e257e81f23812fcf check-python and the fleet preflight now refuse Python 3.10 up front; the toolkit already imports 3.11-only names, so 3.10 failed later anyway, and 3.11 or newer behaves exactly as before
# why: 2026-11-11 76707b774934bb56 acp.py opens an agent's pipes as UTF-8 by name; macOS and Linux read them as UTF-8 already, and a byte that is not UTF-8 is now replaced where it ended the reader
# why: 2026-11-11 ea37558164d2a25f the stand-in agent offers a terminal sign-in only to a client that says it can run one, and refuses a prompt as signed out
# why: 2026-11-11 bad785543f7a5824 the stand-in agent offers a terminal sign-in only to a client that says it can run one, and refuses a prompt as signed out
# why: 2026-11-11 f066e7f867af051c the board's protocol client says it can have a terminal sign-in run, and a fault carries the agent's error code
# why: 2026-11-11 b3631ca06a7c7970 the merge gate's scratch worktree carries the skills extensions install as well as their tools, and a cleared park under a stopped line is carried on mid-turn
# why: 2026-11-11 b19e297951d0d356 the registry names the npm package and the command of each harness's own CLI
# why: 2026-11-12 5a5aaa986729f7a7 main's registry change and this branch's merge-gate fix meet in one merge
# why: 2026-11-13 3b8a61de97e2d746 phase 25.4 (docs/stop-the-line-plan.md), owner's rule 2026-11-13: under /cruise with a deciding `decide`, a late told and the decision ceiling no longer force a boundary. A deliberate behaviour change on every platform, cruise only; outside cruise inbox.py and captain.py behave as before
# why: 2026-11-13 747d8788e453b0ee phase 25.2/25.3 (docs/stop-the-line-plan.md), owner's rule 2026-11-13: a red trunk stops the line and the harbourmaster sends the trunk mender (new scripts/agents/mender.py, harbour lines mend/mended/mend-failed); captains hold on red; broke_it reads the grant. A deliberate behaviour change on every platform; 'mender: off' in harbour.json keeps a red parking for a person
# why: 2026-11-13 d3d6851285dabce5 logs.py: comments only, shortened to its size budget; behaviour unchanged
# why: 2026-11-13 3d2c262c657bc8bb Phase 25.1, the owner's decision of 2026-11-13: every toolkit script reads and writes the run's own state under .slipwai/run/ through logs.run_dir, and the ignore block has one line for it. This is a deliberate path change, not a behaviour-preserving edit: a project whose .gitignore lacks .slipwai/run/ keeps the old places, and slipwai migrate moves the state in.
# why: 2026-11-13 c563d5c8c98b73aa mender.py: the record's dict is built on its own line so the write carries its encoding on one line; behaviour unchanged
# why: 2026-11-13 b4743bd7886552d3 mender.py: a zombie attempt reads as ended where /proc says so, and SLIPWAI_MENDER is split on whitespace like SLIPWAI_SAIL so a Windows path keeps its backslashes; macOS and Linux behave as before for a live or ended attempt

